# ChatGPT desktop uses Work mode

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-10-10):

> **Always use work mode when controlling ChatGPT 6 desktop.**

## The rule

> **Any control of the ChatGPT desktop app uses Work mode. When the app
> shows a Work handoff, accept it. The button is named "Continue in Work".
> Do not decline that handoff. Do not tell the chat to stay out of Work
> mode.**

## Required

1. Before sending a task that must change analoginfo.com or read local
   files, the ChatGPT desktop session must be in Work mode.
2. The moment a button named `Continue in Work` appears, click it.
   Waiting out the prompt declines the handoff.
3. After an accepted handoff, leave Work mode in control of the browser
   and the local files. Do not click the desktop while that computer-use
   session is active.

## Bandwidth

Work mode is not a license to crawl analoginfo.com or Webflow staging.
Local copy first. Named User-Agent. Explicit changed URLs only. See
`public-site-bandwidth-budget.mdc`,
`public-site-no-speculative-crawls.mdc`, and
`public-site-image-weight.mdc`. Do not replay
`bandwidth-20261030-r1`.

## Forbidden

- Declining, dismissing, or timing out the Work handoff.
- Sending "do not use Work mode" or any instruction to stay in ordinary chat.
- Treating the ChatGPT / Codex mode switcher as a substitute. That menu
  does not contain Work. Work is the in-chat handoff.
- Using Work mode to run a full-site audit, WordPress-path probe, or
  sitemap IndexNow dump against analoginfo.com or
  analoginfo-b2base-site.webflow.io.
